TOTK: DontInline on the raw global-memory helpers of OoT's foliage mesh shaders. Eight mesh shaders, 60,288 to 69,376
bytes of code (some 3,800 to 4,300 instructions; 179k to 193k SPIR-V words), call the helpers that
GlobalToStorage.TryGenerateRawStorageOp makes for an address traced to no storage buffer (the memory pool table lookup,
named *Raw) 950 to 982 times, and a driver that inlines every call runs out of registers at 255 and makes 1 to 2 MB of
machine code. Called instead, the forest's foliage takes some 45% less GPU time (about 1.1 ms a frame there). On the
smaller mesh shaders DontInline costs up to 29%, so MeshStage.Large (tools/xlate/Program.cs MakeMeshStage: a code file
of 60,000 to 70,000 bytes) asks for it, and every other shader is translated byte for byte as before. The next mesh
shader that calls the helpers is 46,592 bytes long (283 to 550 calls); the larger ones (184,704 to 294,912 bytes) reach
all their memory through c0 and call none. runtime/nvn_ctl.h nvn2_ctl_mesh_large tests the same length (control +0x38)
and gfx_shader.c build_code_hash tags those programs, which keeps the translator identity (tools/build_xlate.py SAME_AS)
for everything else.

